tools/row-vectors/target/
tools/vxbench-rs/target/
**/Cargo.lock.orig

# ---- Conformance corpus (committed, not generated on the fly) ----
# The pinned golden corpus IS in the repository. It is deterministic (splitmix64 with a recorded
# master seed), hashed file by file in its own manifest, and re-derivable at any time from
# tools/conformance-gen -- so committing it costs ~17 MB packed rather than the 122 MB it occupies
# on disk, and it keeps `dotnet test` working on a bare clone with no Rust toolchain. 54 of the
# unit-test project's files and all of the conformance project's depend on it.
tests/**/golden/

# A .vortex file anywhere else is scratch output and is never committed. The corpus and the forged
# fixtures are the two deliberate exceptions -- the forged one matters: its manifest is tracked, so
# ignoring the file it describes leaves a clone with a manifest pointing at nothing.
*.vortex
!tests/Vorticity.Conformance/corpus/**/*.vortex
!tests/Vorticity.Conformance/forged/**/*.vortex

